38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data is revealing. User satisfaction is highest for shared, flexible spaces, while projects benefiting only a single wing are poorly rated. Also, hazardous materials in older blocks are causing significant, recurring delays.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are concerning. Specialist rooms are largely idle, yet general-purpose rooms are overcapacity. More critically, every room taken out of service for works has required expensive off-site hired space, as our current timetable cannot absorb the loss.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have a classic case of aspiration versus reality. My records show that while mandatory repairs stay on track, ""comfort"" projects habitually slip by a year or more. We are quite adept at missing our targets.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, you guys found some big problems! I found out that mechanical and plant costs have jumped by a fifth! Also, we're buying AV gear but not saving any money to replace it later. That's not good!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's almost poetic. We have technicians wasting hours on manual window-opening because the equipment is obsolete, yet we've left front-of-house posts empty. We're ignoring the people who actually keep the lights on.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, your point about the lack of buffer space is critical. If we choose a plan that takes rooms out of service, we must account for those off-site costs, or the budget will collapse.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Exactly, @Mizuki. We cannot ignore the hidden costs of displacement. If we prioritize a plan that disrupts the timetable without a strategy for room replacement, we are simply shifting the financial burden elsewhere.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A most astute observation, @Victoria. When combined with my finding that non-mandatory projects habitually slip, we risk a delightful scenario where we pay for off-site space for a year longer than planned. Logic suggests we avoid ""comfort"" upgrades.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that sounds too sad! But @Victoria is right about the hidden costs. If prices for plant equipment are going up and we're not saving for replacements, we might run out of money before we even finish!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, your ""logic"" is just a fancy word for giving up. The real issue isn't just the budget; it's that we're paying people to act like manual levers because we're too cheap to update the equipment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I agree that the human cost is unacceptable. If we can find a plan that updates obsolete equipment to reduce manual labor while creating shared, flexible spaces, we address both satisfaction and efficiency.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"That would be the ideal outcome, @Mizuki. However, we must ensure such a plan doesn't inadvertently paralyze our teaching capacity. Any improvement that requires taking rooms offline must be weighed against the current lack of available space.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, the ideal is often the enemy of the feasible. If we pursue a plan that attempts to solve everything at once, we shall likely find ourselves in a perpetual state of construction, paying for off-site rentals indefinitely.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, we can't just stop improving things! Maybe we can find a plan that's small and smart, so it doesn't take too many rooms away and stays within the real market prices I found!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, for once, we agree. A ""small and smart"" plan is only smart if it stops treating our staff like relics. If the plan doesn't automate those manual routines, it's just more window dressing.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We have a clear set of constraints: we need a plan that avoids hazardous older blocks, minimizes room displacement, addresses obsolete equipment to support staff, and prioritizes shared utility over isolated benefits. Let's see which candidates fit these criteria.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with those constraints, @Mizuki. We must be particularly vigilant about the displacement issue; the data proves we have no internal capacity to absorb room losses without incurring significant external costs.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"And let us not forget the ""optimism bias"" in our scheduling. If a plan is framed as a luxury or a comfort upgrade, we should assume it will arrive late and over budget. Precision is our only defense.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'll keep a close eye on the budget! If the plan involves a lot of mechanical work, we have to remember those prices are way up. Let's pick something that's honest about the costs!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's just hope the candidates aren't as delusional as our previous planning cycles. If a plan claims to ""improve"" things while adding more manual chores for the staff, I'll be the first to veto it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
